# Every variable the console reads, with what it is for. There is exactly one, and it is
# read by the dev server rather than by the console.
# Copy to .env.local for local work.
#
# READ THIS FIRST, because this file used to say the opposite. Vite inlines every
# VITE_-prefixed value into the JavaScript bundle as plain text at build time. This product
# ships one image to every company that installs it, so a bundle carrying one company's
# Keycloak issuer is a bundle only that company can install, and nothing about the build
# would say so. The console therefore reads no VITE_ value at all.
#
# Where the issuer and the client id come from instead: the application serves them at
# /api/console.js, reading them through brain.install like every other installation setting,
# and index.html loads that document before the bundle. To point a development console at a
# different realm, set INSTALL_OIDC_ISSUER on the application you are proxying to, not here.
# See src/config.ts and src/brain/console_static.py.
#
# The client id is not here either, and was not before. It is INSTALL_OIDC_CLIENT_ID on the
# application, defaulting to the client the shipped realm defines; see src/auth/constants.ts
# for why the console will not take one from a browser-side setting.

# --- development only ------------------------------------------------------
# Where `npm run dev` proxies /api and /setup. Never inlined into the bundle: this one has
# no VITE_ prefix on purpose, and is read by vite.config.ts in the Node process.
DEV_API_PROXY_TARGET=http://127.0.0.1:8000
